  "summary_text": "Kyle, yesterday was a solid day post-Father's Day across both stores\u2014Port Washington delivered real momentum despite the holiday headwind, while Hicksville showed material strength with its best grooming output in recent weeks.\n\nPort Washington is running hot. You're up 18% week-to-date and flat to plan for the month when adjusted for calendar (actual $67.7K vs. expected $67.2K). More importantly, your groomers crushed it yesterday at $574/groomer-day, 14% above your 30-day baseline, on 6 active bodies. Core grooming revenue jumped 7% and ticket count up 10%\u2014that's volume and velocity working together. One concern: retail fell 9% and add-on attach dropped from 59% to 50%, suggesting either front-of-house focus softened or upsell discipline slipped post-holiday. Restock the X-Small Treat Table (out) and Bully Sticks (backorder) immediately\u2014those are your top movers. Your lapse pool is substantial at $311K annual value; that's a reactivation opportunity if capacity allows.\n\nHicksville's momentum is real but fragile. You're up 6.2% MTD versus plan, and yesterday's $1,310 (up 25%) was driven by strong grooming (+34%) with solid add-on attach recovery (36% vs. 10% prior week). However, today you've only scheduled 1 groomer and tomorrow just 2\u2014that's a steep cliff and will kill this week's revenue trajectory. More strategically, your 12+ week visit-gap bucket is growing (8.4% to 10.2%), which signals customers are stretching intervals. This is stealth churn. You need to reverse that with consistent capacity and proactive outreach to your 58-person lapse pool ($40K value).\n\nToday: Port Washington 5 groomers with 7.0h bathers; Hicksville 1 groomer with 0.0h bathers. Tomorrow: Port Washington 5 groomers/7.0h; Hicksville 2 groomers/0.0h. Next 7 days: 38 combined groomer-days (28 PW, 10 Hicksville), 43 bather hours (PW only)."
